  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "In the Flower Wine Monk’s strength inheritance on Qing Mao Mountain, Fang Yuan digs a dark gold flower bud from soft soil and names it Earth Treasury Flower Gu. The Flower Wine Monk planted it so the Gu inside would wait for the inheritor.",
        "chapters": [
          63
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "inh_flower_wine_monk_inheritance",
          "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_flower_wine_monk"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A second Earth Treasury flower before a grey rock door yields Jade Skin Gu from the same golden nectar method.",
        "chapters": [
          79
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "inheritance-finds",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_jade_skin_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He compares a hibernating Thousand Li Earthwolf Spider cocoon to White Boar Gu taken from Earth Treasury Flower Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          188
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "comparison",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_thousand_li_earthwolf_spider"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Earth treasury flower is a storage Gu. Flower Wine Monk planted it deep in the cave to store several Gu worms Fang Yuan later obtained. In Three Kings blessed land Fang Yuan plants earth treasury flower Gu into mixed toxic soil during experimentation; several plantings fail before one survives a balance of green pool rotten soil and eight desolate blood powder.",
        "chapters": [
          378
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "planting",
